FYI, this change broke the React Aria test suite when running against Canary: https://app.circleci.com/pipelines/github/adobe/react-spectrum/18713/workflows/5e19b423-38fa-414a-85f0-2a63fcd2a5f2/jobs/268672

Was it intentional that this changes the behavior to take the first result of the memo function rather than the second? Changing this broke some code that relied on the most recent call being the current value. The patching of devtools seems fine, but we verified that reverting the change that swapped which instance `nextValue` comes from fixed our tests. i.e. changing it to this:

```patch
- var nextValue = nextCreate();
if (shouldDoubleInvokeUserFnsInHooksDEV) {
  setIsStrictModeForDevtools(true);
  nextCreate();
  setIsStrictModeForDevtools(false);
}

+ var nextValue = nextCreate();
```

We should probably fix our code not to rely on this assumption, and we will, but since canary is used in production by Next.js I feel like this part of the change should be reverted until a major version. Otherwise users will need to sync their next.js, react, and react-aria updates to avoid running into an issue.

